   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2021, the Montenegrin Employers&#x2019; Federation (MEF) endorsed a strategic plan, which defines the priorities of the organisation for the period 2021-2024. The new strategy builds on the key lessons learned from the implementation of the previous strategy (which expired in 2018) and findings of a comprehensive needs assessment and stakeholder analysis conducted between March-June 2021.
The MEF revisited the current vision, mission statement and strategic goals to ensure that it is future fit. Precisely, specific actions were formulated to improve MEF financial performance, optimise management practices and operations, boost its service offer, increase visibility and enhance its technical capacities, among other things (as recommended by the needs assessment). Furthermore, the strategic plan defines MEF policy priorities on creating a more enabling business environment, among which emerging issues such as women and youth entrepreneurship, green economy, digital transformation and corporate social responsibility.
Despite the major delays posed by the crisis, MEF approved the new strategic plan and embarked quickly on a digital transformation process. Precisely, MEF launched a new website in October 2021, which encompasses among other things such innovations as &#x2018;Membership Discount Program&#x2019; and &#x201c;Business to Business Program (which is a networking program)&#x201d;, aimed at boosting MEF value proposition. Furthermore, in November 2021 MEF released its first digital activity report 2020-2021 reflecting also the results of a satisfaction survey among members (conducted in October 2021) and MEF Brand Book (incorporating guidelines and instructions regarding the usage of the MEF logo as well as other brand elements in a consistent and coherent manner), as foreseen in the strategic plan. Between March-June 2021, the ILO, in collaboration with ITC-ILO assisted MEF in carrying out a membership needs assessment and stakeholder analysis to identify the current gaps and challenges and advise on potential areas for improvement. The assessment included 32 virtual in-depth interviews with MEF leadership, senior staff and (board) members, as well as external stakeholders (government officials, trade unions, media representatives, academia and others). The assessment report was used by MEF in revisiting and re-setting its future priorities. Following the needs assessment and MEF commitment to improve its performance, the ILO supported MEF in holding a two-day strategic planning workshop (on 4-5 August 2021) attended by 28 participants and provided guidance throughout the development of the MEF strategy. The ILO made external expertise available to MEF and facilitated the strategic planning sessions and compiled the first draft of the strategy. The ILO  reviewed and improved further the draft strategic document in collaboration with MEF. As a result, MEF was equipped with the knowledge and capacity to develop annual implementation action plans, as well as to develop a new strategic plan in the future.
 In addition, the ILO provided support in digitalising MEF operations and reporting processes. Under the ILO guidance, MEF developed the content of the report, which was further digitalised with external professional support.</narrative>
   </description>
